Compiling util-linux inside /sources

1. Navigate to the sources directory and download util-linux:

`cd /sources`
`curl -O https://mirrors.edge.kernel.org/pub/linux/utils/util-linux/v2.39/util-linux-2.39.3.tar.gz`

2. Extract the archive and enter the build directory:

`tar -xf util-linux-2.39.3.tar.gz`
`cd util-linux-2.39.3`

3. Configure, compile, and install core utilities (mount, fdisk, blkid):

`./configure --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc --disable-chfn-chsh --disable-login --disable-nologin --disable-su --disable-setpriv --disable-runuser --disable-pylibmount --disable-static --without-python`
`make -j$(nproc)`
`make install`

4. Clean up the build directory:

`cd /sources`
`rm -rf util-linux-2.39.3*`
